    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><em>The simplest way to describe the loupain is as a quadrupedal canine that has learned to stand upright. They’re the second most widespread of Ardor’s races, no doubt in part thanks to their natural instincts. ‘Survival’ is probably one of the most common words in loupain philosophical writing across history, no matter their geographical location. Like the quadruped ancestors they come from, they harbor strong loyalties and a desire for order – even if it is solely to their individual selves. Living is important; all else is secondary. This is evident in their customs, their crafts, and their laws.</em></p><p>@UUID[Compendium.immortal-ardor.journals.JournalEntry.HO16IW50jXn58kdN.JournalEntryPage.X4JU4vfBWsDbz4i1]{Loupain}</p><p><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">Special:</span></span><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"> If you are using the Golarion Ancestries rule, you can select any Shoony or Vlaka heritages and ancestry feats (at your GM’s discretion).</span></p>"
